{"characters":[
{"name":"the Chief Executive Lich","role":"antagonist","description":"Edric Thane, the being at the very top of Aeon Holdings. Third son of a minor merchant house and a clerk in life, he died six hundred years ago owing a debt he could not pay, was retained, climbed by reconciling and restructuring, and learned to pool tenure to buy continuance. He now sits neither living nor properly dead in the corner office, sustained by tenure harvested from every soul sent under. He is thorough rather than cruel, and new hires mistake his initials, the CEL, for a department.","goals":"To keep continuing: to sustain himself on pooled tenure, keep the Pipeline running on renewable hope, and avoid the 'onward' he is afraid of. In the opening scenes he summons Milo to take his measure, interested in the clerk who asks why the ledger is clean.","arc":"From untouchable owner of the machine to a clerk undone by a clerk. When Milo hands him the procedurally flawless reconciliation that zeroes his pooled account, he understands it completely, files it correctly, and goes wherever the dead go.","relationships":{"Milo Voss":"Sees his younger self in Milo's appetite for a clean ledger; summons and warns him, and is finally undone by Milo's resignation and reconciliation.","Zara Okafor":"Once her colleague; the target of the organizing she has spent two centuries building toward."},"personality_traits":{"thorough":"Reads the figures personally; knows Milo closed the Bell account in under four minutes.","controlling":"Keeps a single closed ledger on an empty desk, hands folded on it 'as if it might try to leave'.","convinced":"Believes with the total conviction of the converted that hope is a renewable resource meant to be spent.","afraid":"Chose continuance over graduation; he is afraid of the onward."},"voice_characteristics":{"diction":"Formal, archaic, impersonal ('One finds that...', 'I was once possessed of the same appetite'); bureaucratic terms turned into moral verdicts: diligence, appetite, recorded.","rhythm":"Long, balanced periodic sentences that build to an epigrammatic turn ('Four minutes is not diligence, Mr. Voss; four minutes is appetite.').","tics":"Addresses Milo as 'Mr. Voss'; aphorisms about cost and record-keeping; speaks of souls and habits in terms of expense."},"aliases":["Edric Thane","Chief Executive","the CEL","the Lich"]},
{"name":"Milo Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A new hire in Reconciliations. In life a mid-level operations analyst who spent forty-one years cheerfully optimizing processes whose purpose he never questioned, he died mid-sentence on a Tuesday complaining about a meeting. He was retained for his gift for not asking questions and is good at closing accounts and sending souls under.","goals":"To be useful, seen and good at his job: to hit the ground running, log throughput and climb. Then, once he spots the moved tenure, to understand the discrepancy and find the right stakeholder for it.","arc":"From eager, complicit optimizer who likes being good at a terrible job, through the temptation to report the discrepancy and climb, to joining Zara's union of the dead. He hands the Lich his resignation and the reconciliation of every soul sent under, and learns his boredom was 'a wound where his questions used to be'.","relationships":{"Zara Okafor":"His desk neighbor and trainer; he mistakes her courtesy for friendship before realizing it is recruitment, and becomes her partner, the ledger to her organizing.","the Chief Executive Lich":"Summoned by him and stands when told to sit; Milo is what Edric once was, and becomes the clerk who undoes him.","Halvard Bell":"The account he closed in under four minutes, whose moved tenure exposes the harvest.","Old Fen":"A Records colleague whose contentment Milo envies.","Prava":"The caseworker who onboarded him."},"personality_traits":{"eager":"Rolls his chair closer to the partition, asks what a great first quarter looks like.","oblivious":"Laughs at Zara's line because he thinks it is a joke; reads the Lich's summons as a positive career signal.","starting to notice":"Locks the ledger in his drawer without knowing why; refuses the Lich's chair; spots the column where tenure was moved."},"voice_characteristics":{"diction":"Corporate jargon used in total sincerity: 'aligned on expectations', 'circle back', 'low-hanging fruit', 'end-to-end process', 'stakeholder', 'downstream impact'.","rhythm":"Chatty, run-on, upbeat; questions stacked on reassurances; quick hedges ('Not in a weird way').","tics":"Opens with 'So!' or 'Totally, totally'; justifies every question as a way to optimize; cites his previous role's metrics."},"aliases":["Mr. Voss"]},
{"name":"Zara Okafor","role":"deuteragonist","description":"Dead for two hundred and six years after a factory fire, angry for almost all of them. A Reconciliations employee who cannot stop noticing who is getting hurt, she has read the entire contract including the appendices and has known for a century what the Pipeline pipes. Milo's desk neighbor and trainer, with grey eyes 'flat as a filing cabinet'.","goals":"To find leverage against the Pipeline. She has identified Reconciliations as its weak point and recruits Milo to organize a procedurally impeccable work stoppage, a union of the dead.","arc":"From a lone, patient organizer without leverage to someone who, with Milo's ledger, holds the machine to its own word, and gains the one thing two centuries of anger never could: company.","relationships":{"Milo Voss":"Trains him with flat professional courtesy that is really recruitment; teaches him to notice, then offers him the alternative to climbing.","the Chief Executive Lich":"Once his colleague; she has spent two centuries building toward his undoing and warns Milo how to face him.","Old Fen":"His contentment is the thing she most fears."},"personality_traits":{"patient":"Lets Milo sit with his instinct to climb until he cannot stand himself.","guarded":"Does not look up; gives Milo exactly one second of eye contact; her eyes do not change at the discrepancy.","exacting":"Insists on reading every appendix; gives precise, procedural instructions."},"voice_characteristics":{"diction":"Plain, flat, minimal; procedural imperatives; no jargon.","rhythm":"Short declarative sentences and terse commands in threes ('Bring nothing. Sign nothing. If he offers you a chair, stand.').","tics":"Deadpan lines that sound like jokes but are not; returns to the appendices; answers questions with instructions."},"aliases":[]},
{"name":"Halvard Bell","role":"minor","description":"A dentist in life, then a soul in Retention for ninety years, whose contract was restructured at nine one morning. Milo closed his account and he was sent under by lunch; Facilities cleared his desk.","goals":"","arc":"","relationships":{"Milo Voss":"The account Milo closed in under four minutes; the entry where Milo discovers Bell's tenure was moved, not zeroed."},"personality_traits":{},"voice_characteristics":{},"aliases":["Bell"]},
{"name":"Old Fen","role":"supporting","description":"A soul who has been in Records so long that he has begun to file himself. His tragedy is that he is content.","goals":"","arc":"","relationships":{"Zara Okafor":"His contentment is what she most fears.","Milo Voss":"His contentment is what Milo most envies."},"personality_traits":{"content":"Resigned to the system.","absorbed":"Speaks without looking up from his filing."},"voice_characteristics":{"diction":"Plain, wry.","rhythm":"Brief, offhand aphorism.","tics":"Talks without looking up from his work."},"aliases":["Fen"]},
{"name":"Prava","role":"supporting","description":"The intake caseworker who onboarded Milo with practiced warmth. She has onboarded eleven thousand souls, remembers every name, and keeps them in a private ledger she is not permitted to have.","goals":"To hold on to proof that leaving is possible; she weeps silently, off the clock, at each graduation.","arc":"","relationships":{"Milo Voss":"Onboarded him and told him he was retained and a strong culture fit."},"personality_traits":{"warm":"Delivers onboarding 'warmly', in the voice of onboarding everywhere.","secretly grieving":"Weeps at graduations off the clock; keeps the forbidden ledger of names."},"voice_characteristics":{"diction":"Onboarding corporate warmth: 'retained', 'strong culture fit'.","rhythm":"Short, pleasant, scripted sentences.","tics":""},"aliases":[]}
]}
